BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Life of Chuck
DTSTART:20250618T230000Z
DTEND:20250619T011000Z
DTSTAMP:20250618T230000Z
UID:4KKjuT3lnC
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 110 mins (1h50m)\n\nFrom the hearts and minds of Ste
 phen King and Mike Flanagan comes The Life of Chuck\, the extraordinary st
 ory of an ordinary man. This unforgettable\, genre-bending tale celebrates
  the life of Charles 'Chuck' Krantz as he experiences the wonder of love\,
  the heartbreak of loss\, and the multitudes contained in all of us. Toro
 nto International Film Festival 2024 People's Choice Award winner.\n\nhttp
 s://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/life-of-chuck
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jane Austen Wrecked My Life
DTSTART:20250618T231500Z
DTEND:20250619T011000Z
DTSTAMP:20250618T231500Z
UID:xGbWThPrHV
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 94 mins (1h34m)\n\nAgathe (Camille Rutherford) is a 
 hopelessly clumsy yet charming young woman who works in the legendary Shak
 espeare & Co. bookshop in Paris\, while she dreams of being a successful w
 riter\, and of experiencing love akin to a Jane Austen novel\, she finds h
 erself desperately single and plagued by writers block. When Agathe’s be
 st friend (Pablo Pauly) gets her invited to the Jane Austen Writers' Resid
 ency in England\, she finally has her Jane Austen moment…and is caught i
 n a very unexpected romantic triangle. Agathe must let go of her insecurit
 ies to decide what she really wants for herself\, and to achieve her roman
 tic and professional dreams.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/ja
 ne-austen-wrecked-my-life
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Phoenician Scheme
DTSTART:20250618T231500Z
DTEND:20250619T012000Z
DTSTAMP:20250618T231500Z
UID:N6MBqLuPmT
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nThe story of a family and a fami
 ly business. Benicio del Toro plays tycoon Anatole "Zsa-zsa" Korda\, one o
 f the richest men in Europe\; Mia Threapleton is Sister Liesl\, his daught
 er/a nun\; Michael Cera is Bjorn Lund\, an entomologist.\n\nhttps://www.si
 ff.net/cinema/in-theaters/phoenician-scheme
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
