BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Brief History of Contemporary Cinema as Told Through James Bond
DTSTART:20250626T010000Z
DTEND:20250626T025000Z
DTSTAMP:20250626T010000Z
UID:c42pw9M9aD
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nThe world's greatest spy has been
  entertaining film-lovers for over 60 years. In that time\, the art of fil
 mmaking has gone through many changes and has chased many trends. Due to t
 he franchise's longevity - cinematography\, editing\, sound design\, and m
 any other aspects of filmmaking have advanced incredibly (well... mostly).
  Join SIFF Development & Membership Manager Carson Rennekamp on a top secr
 et mission to uncover and examine examples of a shifting film landscape. B
 ecause after all\, nobody does it better. To reserve your free member tick
 ets\, click the "SIGN IN" button in the upper corner of this screen. Once 
 signed in\, click the showtime below to reserve your tickets.\n\nhttps://w
 ww.siff.net/programs-and-events/education/adult-film-education/film-talks/
 members-only-brief-history-of-contemporary-cinema-james-bond
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
